1
00:00:07,560 --> 00:00:08,920
SAY NO TO PIRACY, SUPPORT ORIGINALS

2
00:01:35,520 --> 00:01:38,600
ADAPTED FROM <i>THE EARLY SPRING</i> ON JJWXC.NET
AUTHOR: GU NIANG BIE KU

3
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:41,520
10 MONTHS LATER

4
00:01:46,960 --> 00:01:48,160
<i>Shang Zhitao.</i>

5
00:01:48,240 --> 00:01:50,000
You haven't contacted me
for almost a week.

6
00:01:50,560 --> 00:01:52,760
<i>I told you</i>

7
00:01:52,840 --> 00:01:55,480
that I was conducting a study
in the Gobi Desert with the project team.

8
00:01:55,560 --> 00:01:57,440
The signal over there was bad.

9
00:01:57,520 --> 00:01:59,200
<i>Aren't you going to the US</i>
<i>to report your work?</i>

10
00:01:59,280 --> 00:02:00,800
<i>You haven't left yet?</i>

11
00:02:00,880 --> 00:02:02,120
You're so heartless.

12
00:02:02,920 --> 00:02:05,120
Do you think I can leave
without making sure you're fine?

13
00:02:08,800 --> 00:02:10,800
It's still a long-distance relationship.
Where I'm at makes no difference.

14
00:02:10,880 --> 00:02:12,600
The US and Beijing are the same.

15
00:02:15,600 --> 00:02:16,480
<i>Luan Nian.</i>

16
00:02:17,880 --> 00:02:20,160
I wish you success in your report.

17
00:02:22,560 --> 00:02:23,800
<i>When I'm back home,</i>

18
00:02:23,880 --> 00:02:24,920
let's have a video call.

19
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:25,920
I want to see Luke.

20
00:02:27,400 --> 00:02:28,280
Say it again.

21
00:02:28,360 --> 00:02:30,120
You just want to see Luke?

22
00:02:30,760 --> 00:02:31,880
Of course.

23
00:02:31,960 --> 00:02:33,560
That's my dog.

24
00:02:34,160 --> 00:02:35,440
Say it again.

25
00:02:35,520 --> 00:02:36,520
Whose dog?

26
00:02:37,200 --> 00:02:38,200
Our dog.

27
00:02:44,800 --> 00:02:46,480
<i>Let's leave it here. I'll arrive soon.</i>

28
00:02:56,920 --> 00:02:59,240
I WILL WATCH OVER YOU FROM BEYOND
THIS WORLD, UNTIL YOUR LIFE IS WHOLE

29
00:03:10,160 --> 00:03:11,640
- Thank you.
- Okay.

30
00:03:11,720 --> 00:03:12,680
Tao.

31
00:03:15,400 --> 00:03:16,640
Why are you here?

32
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:21,080
My assignment in Northwestern China
is ending.

33
00:03:22,320 --> 00:03:24,320
I wanted to see you before I leave.

34
00:03:25,080 --> 00:03:26,840
Why didn't you send me a text?

35
00:03:26,920 --> 00:03:28,960
What if you didn't see me?
I just came back from a business trip.

36
00:03:29,920 --> 00:03:32,240
Come up. Let's have a drink.

37
00:03:32,320 --> 00:03:34,800
It's fine. It's quite late.

38
00:03:34,880 --> 00:03:36,120
I have to hurry and catch the last bus.

39
00:03:38,600 --> 00:03:39,520
This is for you.

40
00:03:40,160 --> 00:03:41,360
I got it from the mountains.

41
00:03:41,960 --> 00:03:42,920
I think you might like it.

42
00:03:48,040 --> 00:03:49,800
There was a year

43
00:03:49,880 --> 00:03:53,600
when I received flowers
every day for a week at work.

44
00:03:53,680 --> 00:03:55,040
Was that you?

45
00:03:58,280 --> 00:04:00,960
Back then, you said
you wanted flowers so much,

46
00:04:01,040 --> 00:04:02,440
but if it was prepared beforehand,

47
00:04:02,520 --> 00:04:04,080
it wouldn't be surprising.

48
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:06,480
So, I sent them for a few days as a prank.

49
00:04:08,600 --> 00:04:10,400
I hope you liked them back then.

50
00:04:11,440 --> 00:04:12,400
Thanks, Zhu.

51
00:04:12,480 --> 00:04:13,840
I liked them a lot.

52
00:04:13,920 --> 00:04:15,640
Oh, my work here is done

53
00:04:15,720 --> 00:04:16,560
after a month.

54
00:04:16,640 --> 00:04:17,640
When I return to Beijing,

55
00:04:17,720 --> 00:04:18,760
let's go watch a movie, okay?

56
00:04:18,839 --> 00:04:19,680
Midnight screening.

57
00:04:19,760 --> 00:04:20,800
We'll go every weekend.

58
00:04:20,880 --> 00:04:22,920
Let's watch all the old movies together.

59
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:24,240
We'll call Sun Yu too.

60
00:04:25,360 --> 00:04:26,200
Sure.

61
00:04:26,840 --> 00:04:28,000
I'll buy the tickets.

62
00:04:28,600 --> 00:04:30,080
No. Let Sun Yu buy them.

63
00:04:30,760 --> 00:04:32,560
Her team is doing very well now.

64
00:04:32,640 --> 00:04:34,080
You haven't seen each other for so long.

65
00:04:34,160 --> 00:04:36,960
If Sun Yu knows that you're going back,
she will be so happy.

66
00:04:37,040 --> 00:04:38,880
- Let me tell Sun Yu.
- Don't.

67
00:04:40,400 --> 00:04:41,840
Don't disturb her.

68
00:04:45,360 --> 00:04:46,560
Before you

69
00:04:47,160 --> 00:04:49,960
return to Beijing, do you need
to go back to your hometown?

70
00:04:50,040 --> 00:04:51,400
How's your mother?

71
00:04:51,480 --> 00:04:52,600
Is she doing well?

72
00:04:59,400 --> 00:05:00,240
She passed away.

73
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:07,960
When did that happen?

74
00:05:11,480 --> 00:05:13,000
During the Chinese New Year.

75
00:05:15,120 --> 00:05:15,960
You…

76
00:05:17,160 --> 00:05:18,560
Why didn't you tell us?

77
00:05:21,680 --> 00:05:24,600
That was the time when all of you
were reunited with your family members.

78
00:05:28,680 --> 00:05:30,200
I didn't want all of you to be sad.

79
00:05:41,240 --> 00:05:42,080
What about your younger sister?

80
00:05:43,600 --> 00:05:44,480
Is she well?

81
00:05:45,760 --> 00:05:47,280
She is studying well.

82
00:05:50,040 --> 00:05:50,920
What about your father?

83
00:05:52,960 --> 00:05:53,840
He's doing well too.

84
00:05:57,200 --> 00:05:58,080
What about you?

85
00:05:59,640 --> 00:06:01,000
Are you well, Sun Yuanzhu?

86
00:06:06,360 --> 00:06:07,400
I'm well.

87
00:06:13,240 --> 00:06:14,280
That's good enough.

88
00:06:19,560 --> 00:06:20,720
Let me take you to the bus stop.

89
00:06:20,800 --> 00:06:21,880
I'll drop off my luggage.

90
00:06:21,960 --> 00:06:22,800
Wait for me.

91
00:06:25,160 --> 00:06:26,240
Tao.

92
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:39,000
Actually, I'm unwell.

93
00:06:43,280 --> 00:06:44,520
I'm very sad.

94
00:06:46,240 --> 00:06:48,600
I've put in a lot of effort.
I tried to change.

95
00:06:50,160 --> 00:06:52,360
But no matter what I do,

96
00:06:53,280 --> 00:06:54,600
and how much effort I put into it,

97
00:06:56,880 --> 00:06:59,520
I couldn't achieve the result I wanted.

98
00:07:11,760 --> 00:07:15,360
I've put in 99% effort into it.

99
00:07:16,880 --> 00:07:18,440
Why can't I…

100
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:23,960
get that final 1%

101
00:07:24,040 --> 00:07:25,920
luck?

102
00:07:30,560 --> 00:07:31,800
Don't cry.

103
00:07:38,920 --> 00:07:39,960
It's fine.

104
00:07:58,600 --> 00:08:00,320
Don't cry, all right?

105
00:08:02,320 --> 00:08:04,560
You will get that 1%.

106
00:09:18,960 --> 00:09:19,960
Sun Yu.

107
00:09:22,200 --> 00:09:24,240
Sun Yuanzhu's mother passed away.

108
00:09:29,280 --> 00:09:31,440
<i>He is quite sad. Do you want to visit him?</i>

109
00:09:34,920 --> 00:09:36,160
I'll come tomorrow.

110
00:09:38,040 --> 00:09:39,360
Let me send you the address.

111
00:09:39,440 --> 00:09:40,360
No need.

112
00:09:41,440 --> 00:09:42,880
I've been there many times.

113
00:09:44,160 --> 00:09:46,480
<i>Throughout my whole life,</i>

114
00:09:46,560 --> 00:09:49,680
I've only traveled a long way,
regardless of any obstacles,

115
00:09:50,600 --> 00:09:51,800
again and again for his sake.

116
00:09:55,280 --> 00:09:58,000
Just to have a meal with him

117
00:09:59,800 --> 00:10:00,720
and have a quick chat.

118
00:10:01,920 --> 00:10:02,920
Then,

119
00:10:03,720 --> 00:10:06,280
I'd take the early flight back
the next day.

120
00:10:07,480 --> 00:10:08,520
<i>I'll be there tomorrow.</i>

121
00:10:10,480 --> 00:10:11,320
Okay.

122
00:10:20,520 --> 00:10:25,440
BEIJING TO LANZHOU
FLIGHT TICKET PURCHASE WEBSITE

123
00:10:25,520 --> 00:10:28,360
SELECT PASSENGER: SUN YU

124
00:10:28,440 --> 00:10:30,240
TOTAL: RMB 734, PAY NOW

125
00:10:34,120 --> 00:10:35,440
PAYMENT SUCCESSFUL

126
00:11:00,840 --> 00:11:02,880
SHANG ZHITAO

127
00:11:12,640 --> 00:11:15,640
<i>The number you are calling is busy.</i>

128
00:11:30,920 --> 00:11:33,080
SHANG ZHITAO

129
00:11:38,480 --> 00:11:39,640
Hello?

130
00:11:40,640 --> 00:11:41,480
Luan Nian.

131
00:11:42,560 --> 00:11:43,640
Are you busy?

132
00:11:43,720 --> 00:11:44,560
Right.

133
00:11:45,360 --> 00:11:46,200
I was busy.

134
00:11:46,800 --> 00:11:48,520
<i>Then, I'll video call you tomorrow.</i>

135
00:11:49,200 --> 00:11:50,040
<i>All right?</i>

136
00:11:51,360 --> 00:11:52,600
I'm going to the US
the day after tomorrow.

137
00:11:53,320 --> 00:11:54,800
<i>I'll leave Luke at the pet shop.</i>

138
00:11:54,880 --> 00:11:56,480
I'm returning to Beijing next week.

139
00:11:57,200 --> 00:11:58,040
Okay.

140
00:11:59,880 --> 00:12:00,720
I'm hanging up.

141
00:12:36,600 --> 00:12:39,360
GROUP CHAT: WAS TRACY TALKING ABOUT YOU
AT THE MEETING?

142
00:12:39,440 --> 00:12:41,440
<i>Is she going to be our future lady boss?</i>

143
00:12:46,760 --> 00:12:49,640
<i>In the future, we must be cautious</i>
<i>when we speak in front of Yilia and Luke.</i>

144
00:12:50,720 --> 00:12:52,160
<i>I also heard from our US colleagues</i>

145
00:12:52,240 --> 00:12:53,920
<i>that they go on</i>
<i>this business trip together.</i>

146
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:55,440
<i>They also have meals together often.</i>

147
00:12:57,120 --> 00:12:59,560
<i>Yilia is a woman born in a rich family.</i>

148
00:12:59,640 --> 00:13:01,000
<i>She's a good match for Luke.</i>

149
00:13:02,320 --> 00:13:05,240
<i>I heard Yilia is the daughter of Mr. You,</i>
<i>our biggest client.</i>

150
00:13:05,320 --> 00:13:07,040
<i>Her father likes Luke a lot.</i>

151
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:09,240
<i>He's going to allocate</i>
<i>next year's advertising budget to Lime.</i>

152
00:13:21,760 --> 00:13:22,720
Tao.

153
00:13:22,800 --> 00:13:24,360
Lumi misses you so much.

154
00:13:27,760 --> 00:13:29,240
Shang Zhitao!

155
00:13:30,880 --> 00:13:32,280
You're finally back!

156
00:13:32,360 --> 00:13:34,080
I miss you so much.

157
00:13:34,160 --> 00:13:35,280
Are you staying for good this time?

158
00:13:35,960 --> 00:13:38,640
Next month. I'm coming back
for good next month.

159
00:13:39,680 --> 00:13:43,040
Do you know what kind of life

160
00:13:43,120 --> 00:13:44,040
I was living in Lime

161
00:13:44,120 --> 00:13:45,800
while you were assigned to work abroad?

162
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:50,360
I've not met another coworker like you

163
00:13:50,440 --> 00:13:52,680
who is impressive,

164
00:13:52,760 --> 00:13:56,200
intelligent, and amazing after you left.

165
00:13:56,920 --> 00:13:58,200
Stop praising me.

166
00:13:58,280 --> 00:14:00,640
Without you, who's going to pamper me?

167
00:14:01,640 --> 00:14:02,720
Let me tell you.

168
00:14:02,800 --> 00:14:05,400
You'll soon be promoted
to specialist in Lime.

169
00:14:05,480 --> 00:14:07,360
You might be the one
pampering me in the future.

170
00:14:08,320 --> 00:14:10,440
I'm still preparing my work report.

171
00:14:10,520 --> 00:14:12,960
Let's wait
until the assessment result is out.

172
00:14:13,040 --> 00:14:15,480
I've gone through everything for you.

173
00:14:16,760 --> 00:14:18,000
The judges of the first round

174
00:14:18,080 --> 00:14:19,720
are the bosses of each division

175
00:14:19,800 --> 00:14:21,560
and two former specialists.

176
00:14:22,160 --> 00:14:23,840
Will is mine.

177
00:14:23,920 --> 00:14:26,680
If he dares give you a low score,
I'll not forgive him.

178
00:14:26,760 --> 00:14:29,560
Tracy has been treating you well, right?

179
00:14:29,640 --> 00:14:31,680
I don't have to say
anything more about Luke.

180
00:14:31,760 --> 00:14:33,240
He's fair, just, and open.

181
00:14:33,320 --> 00:14:36,280
So, your promotion to a specialist

182
00:14:36,360 --> 00:14:38,400
is set in stone.

183
00:14:40,240 --> 00:14:41,080
Is Will

184
00:14:42,160 --> 00:14:43,160
yours?

185
00:14:46,400 --> 00:14:48,080
Well, soon.

186
00:14:48,840 --> 00:14:51,400
Soon? I thought he was already yours.

187
00:14:51,480 --> 00:14:53,600
You're so bad. Are you teasing me?

188
00:14:53,680 --> 00:14:55,720
Of course not. I'll buy you coffee later.

189
00:14:55,800 --> 00:14:57,160
That's more like it.

190
00:14:58,280 --> 00:14:59,640
Luke is back. Do you know that?

191
00:15:01,640 --> 00:15:04,480
Isn't Luke staying in the US for a month?

192
00:15:05,440 --> 00:15:06,880
He came back early.

193
00:15:06,960 --> 00:15:08,320
Go and report to him

194
00:15:08,400 --> 00:15:09,840
when he is here later.

195
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:14,840
Specialist.

196
00:15:22,720 --> 00:15:23,560
Luke.

197
00:15:34,800 --> 00:15:36,080
Come in.

198
00:15:40,840 --> 00:15:41,680
You're back.

199
00:15:44,280 --> 00:15:46,560
Why didn't you tell me beforehand?

200
00:15:47,760 --> 00:15:48,960
I made a last-minute change to my plans.

201
00:15:54,880 --> 00:15:55,760
What is it?

202
00:15:57,920 --> 00:15:58,760
No…

203
00:15:59,440 --> 00:16:01,960
It's nothing.
I just came to report to you.

204
00:16:06,880 --> 00:16:07,720
Sure.

205
00:17:00,640 --> 00:17:01,600
Why are you still here?

206
00:17:03,560 --> 00:17:04,680
I'm waiting for you.

207
00:17:21,560 --> 00:17:22,480
What's wrong?

208
00:17:22,560 --> 00:17:24,280
Something bad happened
when you were in the US?

209
00:17:26,960 --> 00:17:27,920
Everything was normal.

210
00:17:29,880 --> 00:17:31,240
We've not seen each other for two months.

211
00:17:31,320 --> 00:17:32,480
Don't you miss me?

212
00:17:32,560 --> 00:17:33,560
I missed you a lot.

213
00:17:35,200 --> 00:17:36,040
Is that so?

214
00:17:38,120 --> 00:17:39,000
I didn't.

215
00:17:43,400 --> 00:17:44,240
What's wrong?

216
00:17:45,680 --> 00:17:46,840
Did I offend you somehow?

217
00:17:46,920 --> 00:17:47,880
You're scaring me.

218
00:17:49,880 --> 00:17:51,160
Me? Scaring you? No way.

219
00:17:52,440 --> 00:17:54,360
You insisted on staying
in Northwestern China.

220
00:17:54,440 --> 00:17:55,360
You said you liked it there.

221
00:17:55,440 --> 00:17:57,000
What's the point of missing you?

222
00:17:57,560 --> 00:17:58,840
I can't transfer you back either.

223
00:17:59,840 --> 00:18:01,880
You have your own definition of success

224
00:18:01,960 --> 00:18:03,640
and your own way of living.
I respect that.

225
00:18:03,720 --> 00:18:05,000
I have no right to interfere.

226
00:18:05,080 --> 00:18:06,640
You have the right
to choose your own life.

227
00:18:06,720 --> 00:18:07,600
No problem.

228
00:18:10,320 --> 00:18:12,360
Can we talk nicely?

229
00:18:12,440 --> 00:18:13,680
What are you trying to say here?

230
00:18:14,600 --> 00:18:15,440
What am I trying to say?

231
00:18:16,560 --> 00:18:18,680
My girlfriend was talking

232
00:18:18,760 --> 00:18:20,400
with another man downstairs

233
00:18:20,480 --> 00:18:21,520
while crying and hugging him
the whole night.

234
00:18:26,400 --> 00:18:27,480
What do you mean?

235
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:29,560
What do you mean by

236
00:18:30,400 --> 00:18:31,760
hugging and crying with someone else?

237
00:18:34,200 --> 00:18:35,720
Shang Zhitao, you're quite something.

238
00:18:36,640 --> 00:18:38,200
You keep saying you miss me,

239
00:18:38,280 --> 00:18:39,920
but you keep looking for your next one.

240
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:42,840
Do you think you are so charming
that you can start fooling around

241
00:18:42,920 --> 00:18:44,320
- with different men?
- Luan Nian.

242
00:18:45,680 --> 00:18:47,120
You can choose not to trust me,

243
00:18:47,200 --> 00:18:48,880
but you cannot accuse me
of something I never did.

244
00:19:00,040 --> 00:19:01,040
Did I confront you about this?

245
00:19:01,720 --> 00:19:03,240
Did I confront you
when you dined with another woman?

246
00:19:03,320 --> 00:19:04,520
I didn't, right?

247
00:19:04,600 --> 00:19:05,520
Did I confront you

248
00:19:05,600 --> 00:19:07,120
about why the company
is full of rumors about you two?

249
00:19:07,200 --> 00:19:09,640
I didn't, right? Because I trust you.

250
00:19:09,720 --> 00:19:12,240
I've always thought that
we knew each other well

251
00:19:12,320 --> 00:19:14,040
in terms of our social circle.

252
00:19:14,120 --> 00:19:16,160
However, you are pinning
such a big accusation on me

253
00:19:16,240 --> 00:19:17,960
because I went to comfort my friend.

254
00:19:18,040 --> 00:19:19,400
Should we just avoid any interactions

255
00:19:19,480 --> 00:19:21,480
with the other gender
because we are together?

256
00:19:21,560 --> 00:19:24,240
No need. I didn't avoid it.

257
00:19:25,600 --> 00:19:27,640
I can also get along well

258
00:19:27,720 --> 00:19:30,240
with women whom I admire
and work well with me.

259
00:19:30,320 --> 00:19:31,160
Even if I get off work,

260
00:19:31,240 --> 00:19:32,520
I don't think
having a meal or having a chat

261
00:19:32,600 --> 00:19:34,160
is a waste of time.

262
00:19:34,240 --> 00:19:35,120
I know.

263
00:19:35,200 --> 00:19:37,320
I know you can admire

264
00:19:37,400 --> 00:19:39,160
someone you admire openly.

265
00:19:39,240 --> 00:19:41,440
I've never felt jealous about it.
It's true.

266
00:19:42,480 --> 00:19:44,600
So, Luan Nian, please view

267
00:19:44,680 --> 00:19:47,600
my relationship
with Sun Yuanzhu rationally.

268
00:19:47,680 --> 00:19:49,560
After all, during a few difficult moments
in my life,

269
00:19:49,640 --> 00:19:50,960
it was him,

270
00:19:51,040 --> 00:19:52,280
Lumi, and Sun Yu who kept me company.

271
00:19:54,320 --> 00:19:56,920
Luan Nian, I want you to know
that no matter how much I love you,

272
00:19:57,000 --> 00:19:59,080
I'd never give up my friends.

273
00:19:59,920 --> 00:20:01,960
I also won't interfere with you
working with Song Ying.

274
00:20:08,360 --> 00:20:10,320
That's a fair exchange.

275
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:12,400
I hope you remember and stick to it.

276
00:22:13,120 --> 00:22:14,840
Were you at Northwestern China that day?

277
00:22:18,880 --> 00:22:20,960
How come you knew Sun Yuanzhu cried?

278
00:22:26,760 --> 00:22:30,160
I would like to know
why you came that day.

279
00:22:30,840 --> 00:22:32,240
I would like to know why you cried.

280
00:22:39,160 --> 00:22:41,080
Sun Yuanzhu's family member passed away.

281
00:22:41,920 --> 00:22:43,240
He was sad.

282
00:22:44,920 --> 00:22:46,200
He seemed off emotionally.

283
00:22:46,760 --> 00:22:49,040
I figured he was ill. He couldn't eat.

284
00:22:50,360 --> 00:22:52,400
I cried because I felt bad.

285
00:22:56,160 --> 00:22:59,960
Luan Nian. He is
a really good friend of mine.

286
00:23:00,040 --> 00:23:02,680
Can you not get the wrong idea about him
and about our friendship?

287
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:09,880
I'll try my best.

288
00:23:13,400 --> 00:23:14,800
So, you were there that day.

289
00:23:15,840 --> 00:23:16,880
Why?

290
00:23:21,840 --> 00:23:23,400
Because I suddenly missed you.

291
00:23:44,600 --> 00:23:47,040
TIANTONG YUAN STATION TIMETABLE

292
00:23:54,760 --> 00:23:56,080
REDEFINING THE ROLE OF THE ACCOUNT MANAGER
